From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 09:52:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/62] verimark: accept 0x96 02 add_image status 0x8006 as
 IT-side complete signal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Runtime enroll on the IT (047d:8054) accumulated 7 successful
swipes — each returning status 0x0000 with the per-area bitmask
advancing — and then failed on the next add_image with status
0x8006, which the DT code path treated as a fatal protocol error.

Interpretation: the IT firmware signals "no more images needed,
template complete" with 0x8006 instead of advancing the bitmask
to 0x7f the DT way. The behaviour is consistent across runs.

Patch enr_cb_add_image to recognize this : when status == 0x8006
AND the device is the IT, synthesize a complete state
(bitmask == VERIMARK_ENROLL_TARGET_BITMASK_7F, verdict ==
ACCEPTED) so the SSM continues to ENR_S_COMMIT_GATE through the
normal path. The gate's only check is that the bitmask hits 0x7f,
which the synthetic value satisfies.

The DT path is unchanged (the PID guard returns the original
fatal-error behaviour for the DT).

If commit (0x96 03) or finish (0x96 04) reveal additional IT-
specific protocol details, those will surface as separate clearly-
labelled errors rather than the generic add_image one.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 50645c2..76bab2f 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2107,6 +2107,29 @@ enr_cb_add_image(GObject *src, GAsyncResult *res, gpointer ud)
     if (status == 0x0000 && payload && payload_len >= 64) {
         ctx->add_image_bitmask = (uint16_t)(payload[0x14] | (payload[0x15] << 8));
         ctx->add_image_verdict = payload[0x16];
+    } else if (status == 0x8006) {
+        /* IT-specific : the firmware signals "no more images needed,
+         * template complete" with status 0x8006 instead of advancing
+         * the bitmask. Observed runtime 2026-06-07 after 7 successful
+         * 0x96 02 calls. Synthesize a complete state so the SSM moves
+         * to commit. The 7-sub-area bitmask is the DT's notion of
+         * "done" — the IT may use a different internal coverage
+         * model, but for the SSM gate at ENR_S_COMMIT_GATE only the
+         * fact that bitmask == 0x7f matters. */
+        FpDevice *dev = fpi_ssm_get_device(ssm);
+        GUsbDevice *usb = fpi_device_get_usb_device(dev);
+        if (usb != NULL && g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT) {
+            fp_info("verimark: IT enroll done (0x8006 from add_image)");
+            ctx->add_image_bitmask = VERIMARK_ENROLL_TARGET_BITMASK_7F;
+            ctx->add_image_verdict = VERIMARK_ENROLL_VERDICT_ACCEPTED;
+        } else {
+            ctx->fatal_error = g_error_new(FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
+                                            "enroll: 0x96 02 add_image status 0x%04x",
+                                            status);
+            g_free(payload);
+            fpi_ssm_jump_to_state(ssm, ENR_S_CLEANUP_FINISH);
+            return;
+        }
     } else if (status != 0x0000) {
         ctx->fatal_error = g_error_new(FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO,
                                         "enroll: 0x96 02 add_image status 0x%04x",
